<GuideLayout 
  title="Maximum Support: Designing High-Impact Sport Bras" 
  type="PRODUCT GUIDE"
  description="Explore construction techniques for high-impact support. From molded cups to adjustable straps, learn how to build the perfect sport bra."
>
  <h2>The Engineering of Support</h2>
  <p>Designing a sport bra for high-impact activities like running or HIIT requires a balance of encapsulation, compression, and comfort. At Fitclo, we specialize in technical construction that minimizes bounce without sacrificing style.</p>
  
  <h3>Key Functional Elements</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Encapsulation vs. Compression:</strong> We offer both. Compression is great for A/B cups, while encapsulation (molded cups) provides superior support for C+ sizes.</li>
    <li><strong>Power Mesh Lining:</strong> Integrated in the wings and back to provide firm hold while maintaining breathability.</li>
    <li><strong>Reinforced Straps:</strong> Wider, padded straps distribute weight evenly and prevent digging into the shoulders during intense movement.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Performance Fabrics</h3>
  <p>For high-impact bras, we recommend high-density Interlock fabrics (280-320 GSM). These provide the necessary tensile strength to maintain the bra's shape and support level over time.</p>

  <h3>Customization Options</h3>
  <p>From custom-branded elastic underbands to laser-cut ventilation and reflective logos, we can customize every aspect of your sport bra line to stand out in the competitive 2026 market.</p>
</GuideLayout>
